+# Front office decision follow-through — build 2246
+
+This update extends the existing Front Office Brief, prepared My Team need handoff, Trade workspace, exact protections, comparisons and franchise-history view. It adds no parallel navigation or recommendation engine.
+
+## Confirmed boundaries and corrections
+
+- Home previously sent every diagnosed position to Depth and followed dictionary insertion order within needs. The existing `prepared_need` selector already admits a matching current league/franchise/week/generation and prioritizes a starter need before depth. Reuse its fingerprinted handoff and editable filter; provisional or unmatched evidence keeps the ordinary inspection link.
+- A saved goal with no prepared sources previously yielded an empty brief indistinguishable from no actionable opportunities. An informational preparation action names the evidence gap without converting it into roster weakness or starting preparation on Home.
+- Recommended's completed response previously copied search-only protected assets into the legacy draft constraint list. Clearing search controls could leave an unrelated Evaluate offer blocked. Preserve the applied search snapshot while keeping these two state boundaries separate.
+- Reload qualified comparison snapshots as retained, but persisted-page Back did not. Restore each context and retained label on that path too; preserve ordered packages and refresh only the existing display.
+- Existing account activation caught the deferred subtype as a generic preparation error. Preserve typed waiting and already-supported retry semantics; prospective logs use only the guard plan/cleanup values already calculated.
+
+## Responsiveness validation
+
+The earlier complete local run failed its unchanged 100 ms lightweight-request assertion at 157.623 ms. It remains failed; an isolated passing rerun is not release acceptance. A matched rooted, GC-tracked old-heap control reproduced a 186.369 ms failure including 184.088 ms automatic generation-1 collection before the lightweight ASGI handler. Explicit setup collection before the timer yielded a 1.475 ms request with the same retained graph, enabled/default GC and genuinely pending audit worker. A real 120 ms blocking handler still failed at 121.965 ms. No timeout, worker wait or threshold changed. This demonstrates a causal fixture mechanism; it cannot retroactively prove an unrecorded GC event in the historical 157.623 ms sample.
+
+The narrow test change settles setup allocations outside the measured request. It does not change production garbage collection, claim general application latency improved or replace the required final full local canonical run. Original failing traces, setup/negative controls and full-suite results remain separately identified.
+
+## Required final acceptance
+
+Exercise the complete existing Home → editable Trade need → explicit protected search → two independently prepared evaluations/keep-roster comparison → partner history → contextual return journey in one-QB/FLEX/K/DEF and Superflex fixtures. Record actual outgoing identities and qualified versus exploratory outcomes. No results is legitimate and cannot prove protection exclusion. Check controls, changed/applied settings, reload, Back, replacement/removal, league switching, keyboard/touch and 320×432, 375×667, 390×844 and desktop layouts. Opening pages or disclosures must not start unrequested heavy work.
+
+A release requires the full canonical ten-gate validator, all required hosted jobs, native resource/lifecycle controls, exact source/tree and original artifact integrity, and the guarded Actions publisher. Counts and outcomes belong in the completed evidence, not inferred from this document.
+
+## Live limits and preserved contracts
+
+Use only existing authorized owner access and fresh resource evidence for one conditional normal league entry and one explicit protected search. Stop on deferral. Do not force synchronization, clear caches, restart services or manufacture a returned offer. Fixture/replay behavior is separate from live owner acceptance and physical iPhone/Safari testing.
+
+The effective 2 GiB cap, 16× restoration allowance, FOIS 768 MiB and Trade 256+128 MiB reserves, lifecycle ownership and admission rechecks remain unchanged. Preserve source identity, exact pick/original-franchise ownership, account scope, saved rankings/goals/method, Neutral/Custom independence, independent legal pre/post analytical lineups, submitted Sleeper lineups and historical FOIS qualifications. Historical tendencies describe observed records, not present private intent.
